  "source": "claude_session",
  "raw_text": "A resumable batch driver, tag_store.py, was built to close the gap that had previously capped progress and made partial runs indistinguishable from complete ones. The driver runs fused logos then conflict per inference, skips already-complete inferences, writes state after each sub-step into the inference files themselves via a _tagged marker rather than a new database, fails fast on transport-down with exit code 3 so a re-run resumes where it stopped, records per-inference content errors without sinking the batch, and writes a completeness manifest. cross_scale was wired to read that manifest and warn loudly on a half-tagged store, eliminating the trap where a partial result looked real.",
